WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.050 --> 00:00:01.338
Why modernize now?

2
00:00:01.338 --> 00:00:03.662
Start with what the
directory has been doing.

3
00:00:03.662 --> 00:00:07.960
Most federal estates still run
the client/server model they built

4
00:00:07.960 --> 00:00:12.101
in the early 2000s, with an Active
Directory forest at the center.

5
00:00:12.101 --> 00:00:16.238
Since Windows 2000, the organizational
unit has grouped objects

6
00:00:16.238 --> 00:00:20.300
for delegating administrative
rights and assigning policies.

7
00:00:20.300 --> 00:00:23.338
So placing a user or
computer in the tree decided

8
00:00:23.338 --> 00:00:26.300
several things at once,
with no separate record.

9
00:00:26.300 --> 00:00:29.362
Who administers it, through
the permissions on the OU.

10
00:00:29.362 --> 00:00:34.863
Which policy applies, through Group
Policy linked to sites, domains and OUs.

11
00:00:34.863 --> 00:00:37.187
What it can reach,
through group membership.

12
00:00:37.187 --> 00:00:41.101
How it's named, through DNS
zones stored in the directory.

13
00:00:41.101 --> 00:00:45.225
And whether it's trusted, through
certificates enrolled by Group Policy.

14
00:00:45.225 --> 00:00:46.437
None of that was wrong.

15
00:00:46.437 --> 00:00:48.163
It just was never written down.

16
00:00:48.163 --> 00:00:50.176
And the cloud doesn't inherit it.

17
00:00:50.176 --> 00:00:53.339
Entra ID's administrative
units can't be nested,

18
00:00:53.339 --> 00:00:57.638
and policy is assigned to groups,
not inherited from a container.

19
00:00:57.638 --> 00:01:01.364
An agency that moves the users
and retires the forest without

20
00:01:01.364 --> 00:01:05.163
recovering those decisions
doesn't modernize its governance.

21
00:01:05.163 --> 00:01:06.260
It deletes it.
